-- KNOWN GAP, not a discovery: InstanceTable's own record_entries (this
-- session's own addition) keys a record instance target purely on its
-- sorted field-*name* set, not field *types* -- documented at the time in
-- that field's own doc comment as an accepted limitation, not an
-- oversight. IntBox and StringBox are genuinely different, unrelated
-- record shapes (one wraps an Int, the other a String) that happen to
-- share the single field name `value` -- declaring Show for both in the
-- same module collides as a false-positive DuplicateInstance, purely
-- because "which fields does this record have" is the only handle left
-- once type-alias expansion has already erased both names down to their
-- literal record shape. See checker_impl_summary.md's own "Known gaps"
-- section. Expected once fixed (needs field-type-aware keying, not
-- attempted here): both instances accepted, no error at all.
type alias IntBox = { value : Int }
type alias StringBox = { value : String }

instance Show IntBox where
  show b = "int:" <> show b.value

instance Show StringBox where
  show b = "str:" <> b.value
